 # Add --desc support to task create
 
-
+# sandpiper-tasks CLI: accept `--desc` on `task create`
+
+**Route to:** `sandpiper-ai` repo (owner of the tasks skill + CLI).
+
+## Symptom
+
+Agents using the tasks skill for the first time in a session consistently hit:
+
+```
+error: unknown option '--desc'
+```
+
+…when they try to create a task with both a title and a description in one call:
+
+```bash
+sandpiper-tasks task create -p STD -t "Foundations" --priority HIGH --reporter USER \
+  --desc "Establish the XDG-based path layout..."
+```
+
+The fallback they learn is: create without a description, then run `task update <key>
+--desc "..."` as a second call. For a session that's decomposing a project into
+well-scoped tickets, this doubles the CLI invocation count (12 calls for 6 tickets
+instead of 6).
+
+The user reports seeing this "a LOT the first time agents use Tasks in a session" —
+it's the single most common friction point on first contact with the skill.
+
+## Root cause: this is both a doc issue and a missing affordance
+
+### Doc contribution
+
+The current `SKILL.md` in the `Common Operations` section shows `--desc` prominently
+on `task update`:
+
+```
+scripts/sandpiper-tasks task update SHR-1 --desc "New description text"  # set description
+```
+
+…but silently omits it from the `task create` examples, and doesn't tell the reader
+it isn't accepted there:
+
+```
+scripts/sandpiper-tasks task create -p SHR -t "Implement feature X" --priority HIGH --reporter USER
+```
+
+Because `-t/--title` is parallel between `create` and `update`, the natural inference
+is that `--desc` is too. The doc teaches a wrong mental model by omission.
+
+### Missing affordance
+
+Semantically, a description is part of a task's initial content, not a mutation.
+The "create + immediately set description" flow is the common case for any session
+decomposing scoped work into tickets. There's no principled reason `task create`
+shouldn't accept `--desc` — the activity log already treats creation specially
+(no "description added" entry), so accepting a description at creation time
+requires no new semantic handling.
+
+## Proposed fix
+
+### CLI
+
+- Source: `~/git/sandpiper-ai/packages/sandpiper-tasks-cli/src/commands/task-create.ts`
+- Add `--desc <description>` option to the `task create` command definition.
+- When provided, write the description into the initial task file body at creation
+  time (same representation used by `task update --desc`). No activity log entry.
+- Add a test in the neighboring `task-subcommands.test.ts` (or sibling test file) for
+  create-with-description.
+
+### SKILL.md docs
+
+- Source: `~/git/sandpiper-ai/skills/sandpiper/tasks/SKILL.md` (NOT `dist/`)
+- Update the `Create a task` example block to show `--desc` usage on one of the
+  examples.
+- Consider adding a one-line note in the `Create a task` block explicitly stating
+  that `--desc` and the relationship flags (`--depends-on`, `--blocked-by`,
+  `--related`) can be set at creation time — these are currently all "update-only"
+  in the mental model the doc conveys.
+
+### Built skill artifact
+
+After updating source, rebuild so `dist/skills/sandpiper/tasks/SKILL.md` reflects
+the change. The user's `~/.claude/skills/tasks` symlinks into `dist/`, so changes
+to the source don't reach Claude Code sessions until the rebuild runs.
+
+## Priority
+
+Low-risk, high-value. Touches one command's option surface + one doc block. Removes
+the single most common first-session faceplant on this skill.
+
+## Reporter
+
+Filed by an agent session in another project on 2026-04-17,
+after hitting this exact pattern while creating 6 top-level STD tasks with
+descriptions.
+
